          "path": "_m/u/9/j/k/pripyat-abandoned-wk/morphological-anomaly-of-scots.jpg",
          "filename": "Morphological anomaly of Scots Pine (Pinus sylvestris) near Pripyat.jpg",
          "caption": "A Scots Pine (Pinus sylvestris) exhibiting an atypical crown shape, photographed near the abandoned city of Pripyat (Chornobyl Exclusion Zone). The tree shows a loss of apical dominance, resulting in a multi-stemmed, bush-like structure. Such morphological anomalies are frequently observed in conifers within the Zone and can be attributed to the effects of ionizing radiation on meristematic tissues (buds) during growth, or potentially biotic stress factors.",
